--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE / APPROACH
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web source is a presentational card (manifest route = "(unrouted)"): the
/automations page maps one Automation row + the live isFiring flag + an optional
vehicleName into the card's props and supplies four callbacks (onToggle /
onReEnable / onDelete / onTestRun). It performs no I/O and uses only
useTranslation. Manifest record requires PARITY 21 = 1 panel (GlassPanel1) +
1 state (success) + 19 strings.

The canonical native card is already shipped + tested at
TeslaSync/feature-views/AutomationCard.{swift,Model,Views,Adapter,strings,
Previews,Tests} (predecessor P4 0082): the full GlassPanel card with the header
(name + status badge + live Firing chip + description), the pin/toggle/kebab
control cluster (incl. the auto-disabled-only Re-enable), the vehicle row, the
run-stats row, the auto-disabled warning, the conflict callouts, the destructive
delete .alert, every load/empty/error/loaded state, the live/stale/offline
freshness downgrade, VoiceOver labels, and the 19 web i18n keys. This P7 PAGE
unit ships the standalone, deep-linkable SwiftUI SCREEN that hosts that card
through an @Observable model + a NavigationDestination seam — REUSING the card
(DRY; no second copy), exactly mirroring the accepted sibling
page:automations/AutomationActivityFeed (Page + PageModel + RouteRegistration in
Sources/Features/Automations, tests in Tests/Unit/Features/Automations).

OUTPUT-PATH DEVIATION (recorded — no silent drift): the generated prompt names
apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Automations/** (a path that does not exist in this
repo). The real, XcodeGen-enumerated conventions are Sources/Features/<Domain>/**
(pages) + Tests/Unit/Features/<Domain>/** (co-located XCTest), which is what the
two sibling P7 automations pages used and were accepted under. Files shipped
there; both source roots compile into the single TeslaSync module
(project.yml), so the page reuses the feature-view card directly.

